{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLvYHKBz83qes5rS6QiF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `review --scope repo --no-verify --format json` sends the manifest in the finder user prompt, offers the exploration tools, and the fake receives two finder requests for a script that reads a file and then submits.\n[x] `meta.json` records `scope.survey: true`, `digests.input_kind: \"manifest\"`, and budgets `max_turns: 40` when `--max-turns` is not given; `--max-turns 5` is honored.\n[x] A converged clean survey reports `review_kind: \"survey_triage\"`, `completion: \"complete\"`, `stop_reason: \"converged\"`, and assessment `NO_FINDINGS_IN_SAMPLED_AREAS`.\n[x] A survey cut off by the token budget reports `completion: \"partial\"` with the budget stop reason and exits 4.\n[x] A non-survey review's JSON carries none of the survey fields.\n[x] `--scope repo` in a repository with no commits exits 0 with `NO_DIFF` and writes no run directory.\n[x] lint, typecheck, and the TS test suite pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\n`npx roast review --scope repo` now works end to end, and every checklist item in ticket 25 is checked. The final gate passed: lint is clean, `npm test` passed 6725 of 6725 (typecheck included), and `go build` and `go test ./...` pass.\n\n**Code changes:**\n- **`src/scope/survey.ts` (new):** `buildSurveyRepo` lists the committed files at HEAD rather than the index, then applies `--paths`, the excludes and the linguist exclusions. When the working tree is dirty it adds the two documented notes and stops using the linguist exclusions. It then builds the manifest in the same layout as Go. `manifestQuote` quotes any unsafe name the way Go's `strconv.Quote` does and escapes `<` and `>` as `\\x3c` / `\\x3e`. When any name was quoted, the manifest ends with the explanation line.\n- **`src/scope/build.ts`:** `scope: \"repo\"` now calls the survey code instead of throwing \"not yet supported\".\n- **`src/gocompat/strings.ts`:** `isGoPrint` is now exported so the survey code can reuse it.\n\nThe survey parts of `src/cli/review.ts`, the survey prompt, `renderFinderUser` and `submitDescription(true)` were already written in ticket 20, so I didn't change them. The new CLI tests run through all of them.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `test/scope/survey.ts` calls `build()` against temporary Git repos and covers each scope item, plus a table of `manifestQuote` cases.\n- `test/cli/review-survey.ts` covers the CLI items, including a token-budget cutoff (exit 4, `partial`) and a repo with no commits (`NO_DIFF`, no run directory).\n\nThe survey code was already written when I added most of the scope tests, so they passed on their first run instead of failing first. To check they still catch real bugs, I broke `survey.ts` on purpose: the tests failed, and I restored the file. The CLI tests had 10 failures against the old `build.ts` and pass now.\n\nI added a short note on the survey code to `docs/agents/scope-context.md`. My working notes are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":136923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1075},"output_tokens":789,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"353ea1ad-3c3b-4cd2-b9e9-03deb7fc62de","uuid":"83d4ec86-684c-4e16-811b-8d2ff6160e01","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:57:52.545Z","request_id":"req_011ChLvYHAWfRa9b5xCAu4JA"}
